WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.330
It was on christmas eve day December 24th
during Columbus’s first voyage to the Americas

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:14.110
that one of his ships the Santa Maria drifted
onto a bank due to the fact that the helmsman

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:19.000
thinking the seas were calm enough, gave the
control of the tiller to one of his young

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.000
subordinates.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.279
This had proven to be a huge mistake as the
boy managed the run the boat across some shallow

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:27.600
waters where it got permanently stuck and
damaged.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.099
This happened to occur off the coast of today’s
northern Haiti and so the expedition decided

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:36.700
to to go ashore and seek help from the local
Arawak people who where a subgroup of the

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.650
brother Taino people which inhabited the Caribbean.

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:43.390
They soon came in to contact with the ruler
of the Marien Chiefdom, Guacanagari.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:48.460
He wasn’t the only chief in Hispaniola as
the island was divided in to 5 chiefdoms,

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.170
however he was the only one who mattered to
the Europeans at the moment.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:56.680
After talking to Guacanagari, as Columbus’s
son recalls, the chief and the people were

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.280
extraordinarily nice.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:03.040
More than happy to help out giving the Spaniards
large canoes, storage houses and man power

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.070
to salvage and store whatever they could get
from the immobile ship.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:11.420
Afterwards Guacanagari along with multiple
traders from the surrounding tribes meat with

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.450
Columbus himself.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:17.560
During the conversation the traders enthusiastically
traded all their gold for the Spaniards eagle

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.470
bells as they were fascinated with the sound
they made.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:25.000
After seeing the amount of gold that the local
people possessed and the promise of Guacanagari

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.749
to get more from the Cibao mountains located
in today's Dominican Republic, Columbus decided

00:01:29.749 --> 00:01:34.450
that the imobel Santa Maria and it’s saved
cargo be dismantled and use for construction

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:39.290
of a colony where he will leave the men which
are most important in setting up such colony

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:46.149
i.e. carpenters, physicians, taylors etc.
in total 36 men were left behind.

00:01:46.149 --> 00:01:50.530
This colony which was named La Navidad was
to wait for Columbus’s return all while

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.819
gathering information on the New World and
trading with the local natives largely for

00:01:54.819 --> 00:01:55.819
gold.

00:01:55.819 --> 00:01:59.890
Before Columbus’s departure Guacanagari
assured Columbus that if anything were to

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:04.579
happen to his men he will help out the Christian
colony in any way he can.

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:09.009
Columbus thanked Guacanagari and also ordered
his man that if anything ill faded where to

00:02:09.009 --> 00:02:13.820
acure that they drop all their gold into the
constructed wooden fortress’s well as to

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.120
be found by Columbus when he returns.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:22.330
Now with the first ever European colony established
in the New World columbus set sail back to

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.330
Europe.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.659
A year later in 1493 Columbus returned from
Spain to the town of La Navidad where upon

00:02:27.659 --> 00:02:33.459
entering the town harbor found the entire
colony burned down with no gold and no survivors.

00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:38.060
Confused and horrified by the site Columbus
ordered his men to check for bodies and look

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:40.900
in the fortress’s well for the missing gold.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:45.200
There was no gold in the well but several
dead bodies of the colonists were found in

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:46.530
a nearby field.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:50.230
This however still did not explain what happened
to the entire colony.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:55.360
Then suddenly the brother of Guacanagari accompanied
by several other natives appeared and wished

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.189
to speak to Columbus.

00:02:57.189 --> 00:03:00.299
Upon hearing his story it all became clear.

00:03:00.299 --> 00:03:04.099
After Columbus's departure the men of the
La Navidad quickly started to mingle with

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:09.420
the local women living with 4 or 6 woman at
once, Most of them also started to hord larger

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:14.569
and larger stashes of gold oftentimes bartering
for gold behind each others backs.

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:19.019
Soon the competition between getting more
women and more gold turn into frequent arguments

00:03:19.019 --> 00:03:22.659
and It became so bad that some of the colonists
started to kill each other.

00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:27.270
With all this chaos and hostility in the colony
some of the spaniards decided to leave for

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:30.300
the mountains where they heard the golden
mines where located.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:35.280
They most likely entered the neighboring chiefdom
of Magua which angered the local ruler killing

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.609
all of the Spaniards that dared to come for
his gold.

00:03:38.609 --> 00:03:43.689
Outraged by the actions of the colonists the
ruler organized a full on military attack

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:46.709
on La Navidad to get rid of the remaining
Europeans.

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:51.890
When the attack came, La Navidad was defended
by only 11 men with everyone else either dead

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:56.760
or fleeing with all their gold and wives to
other tribes perhaps even on a different islands.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:02.010
However the 11 Spaniards weren’t alone because
Guacanagari honored his promise to Columbus

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:12.620
and with his men joined in the defence of
the colony.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:19.989
But they were still extremely outnumbered
and after a some fearsome fighting the colony

00:04:19.989 --> 00:04:26.000
just got overwhelmed by the sheer number of
attackers.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.500
All remaining europeans along with some of
Guacanagari’s men were slaughtered and the

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.710
entire colony got set on fire.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:37.200
Guacanagari himself managed to escape but
was injured and that is why his brother came

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.810
to visit Columbus as Guacanagari was unable
due to his injuries.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:46.650
Columbus uphold by his men's actions later
thanked Guacanagari personally for honoring

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:51.530
his promise after which the two exchange gifts
and Columbus went on to try to settle other

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.970
areas of Hispaniola.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:58.330
And so goes the disasters story of the First
ever European colony in the New World.

